7.1) Tight Coupling and Loose Coupling
      * Coupling refers to how closely connected different components or systems are

      Tight Coupling
      --------------
            Tight coupling describes a scenario where software components are highly dependent on each other
            - Class are highly dependent on each other
            - Changes in one class affect another class
            - Hard to maintain and test
            - Less flexible
            - Not recommended in modern application

      Loose Coupling
      --------------
            Loose coupling descibes a scenario where software components are less dependent on each other
            - Classes are less dependent on each other 
            - Changes in one class have minimal impact on others
            - Easy to maintain and test
            - More flexible
            - Recommended in Spring Boot Application

            Achieve Loose Coupling
            ---------------------
                  In Spring Boot, We achieve loose coupling mainly by:
                  - Using Interfaces
                  - Dependency Injection (DI)
                  - Constrcutor Injection
                  - @Autowired Annotation
      
      
